(Title) Tj
T*
(Protocol for an 8-week evaluation of Baduanjin practice combined with computerized) Tj
T*
(cognitive remediation in hospitalized schizophrenia: methods and theoretical framework) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Schizophrenia remains a major source of disability globally, with limited pharmacological) Tj
T*
(impact on cognitive deficits and functional outcomes beyond symptom suppression.) Tj
T*
(Integration of mind-body practices with cognitive rehabilitation may address these gaps.) Tj
T*
(This protocol describes a randomized trial comparing combined Baduanjin \(traditional) Tj
T*
(Chinese mind-body exercise\) and computer-assisted cognitive remediation versus cognitive) Tj
T*
(remediation alone. Participants will be 120 hospitalized patients aged 29-64 with) Tj
T*
(schizophrenia. The combined-intervention arm will receive 85-minute sessions \(40 minutes) Tj
T*
(Baduanjin, 45 minutes computerized cognitive tasks\) five days per week for 8 weeks.) Tj
T*
(Control participants receive identical computerized cognitive work without movement) Tj
T*
(training. Measurements occur at baseline and week 8, assessing psychiatric symptoms) Tj
T*
(\(PANSS\), neurocognitive performance \(NCSE\), social functioning \(SSPI\), and subjective) Tj
T*
(quality of life \(SQLS\). Intent-to-treat analysis will evaluate intervention efficacy on) Tj
T*
(symptom severity and functional domains.) Tj
